text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'Add {B} for each creature card in your graveyard.', 'Add {B}{B}{B}.', 'All creatures lose flying until end of turn.\\nSacrifice a snow land: Return Whiteout from your graveyard to your hand.', 'All lands are no longer snow.', "Arctic Foxes can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or greater as long as defending player controls a snow land.", "As Call to Arms enters the battlefield, choose a color and an opponent.\\nWhite creatures get +1/+1 as long as the chosen color is the most common color among nontoken permanents the chosen player controls but isn't tied for most common.\\nWhen the chosen color isn't the most common color among nontoken permanents the chosen player controls or is tied for most common, sacrifice Call to Arms.", "As Lost Order of Jarkeld enters the battlefield, choose an opponent.\\nLost Order of Jarkeld's power and toughness are each equal to 1 plus the number of creatures the chosen player controls.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, pay 3 life.\\nDestroy target creature and target land.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, pay X life.\\nFire Covenant deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of target creatures.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nAdd X mana in any combination of {B} and/or {R}, where X is the sacrificed creature's mana value.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nSearch your library for a creature card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "As long as it's your turn, creatures you control get +2/+0.\\nAs long as it's not your turn, creatures you control get -0/-2.", 'At end of combat, destroy all creatures blocking or blocked by Kjeldoran Frostbeast.', 'At end of combat, put a paralyzation counter on each creature blocking or blocked by Dread Wight and tap those creatures. Each of those creatures doesn\'t untap during its controller\'s untap step for as long as it has a paralyzation counter on it. Each of those creatures gains "{4}: Remove a paralyzation counter from this creature."', 'At the beginning of each end step, if a creature dealt damage by Krovikan Vampire this turn died, put that card onto the battlefield under your control. Sacrifice it when you lose control of Krovikan Vampire.', "At the beginning of each player's end step, tap all untapped Islands that player controls and Monsoon deals X damage to the player, where X is the number of Islands tapped this way.", 'At the beginning of each upkeep, count the number of permanents. If the number is odd, until end of turn, red creatures get +1/+1 and whenever a player taps a Mountain for mana, that player adds an additional {R}. If the number is even, until end of turn, red creatures get -1/-1 and if a player taps a Mountain for mana, that Mountain produces colorless mana instead of any other type.', 'At the beginning of the end step, if no creatures are on the battlefield, sacrifice Withering Wisps.\\n{B}: Withering Wisps deals 1 damage to each creature and each player. Activate no more times each turn than the number of snow Swamps you control.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, Minion of Tevesh Szat deals 2 damage to you unless you pay {B}{B}.\\n{T}: Target creature gets +3/-2 until end of turn.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, for each player, Lim-Dûl's Hex deals 1 damage to that player unless they pay {B} or {3}.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a time counter on Infinite Hourglass.\\nAll creatures get +1/+0 for each time counter on Infinite Hourglass.\\n{3}: Remove a time counter from Infinite Hourglass. Any player may activate this ability but only during any upkeep step.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a time counter on Time Bomb.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Time Bomb: Time Bomb deals damage equal to the number of time counters on it to each creature and each player.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Drought unless you pay {W}{W}.\\nSpells cost an additional "Sacrifice a Swamp" to cast for each black mana symbol in their mana costs.\\nActivated abilities cost an additional "Sacrifice a Swamp" to activate for each black mana symbol in their activation costs.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Earthlink unless you pay {2}.\\nWhenever a creature dies, that creature's controller sacrifices a land.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Glaciers unless you pay {W}{U}.\\nAll Mountains are Plains.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Justice unless you pay {W}{W}.\\nWhenever a red creature or spell deals damage, Justice deals that much damage to that creature's or spell's controller.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice two Swamps. If you can't, tap Infernal Denizen, and an opponent may gain control of a creature you control of their choice for as long as Infernal Denizen remains on the battlefield.\\n{T}: Gain control of target creature for as long as Infernal Denizen remains on the battlefield.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may have Shyft become the color or colors of your choice. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Attacking creatures get +1/+0 and gain trample until end of turn.', 'Balduvian Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+0 counters on it.\\nRemove a +1/+0 counter from Balduvian Hydra: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to Balduvian Hydra this turn.\\n{R}{R}{R}: Put a +1/+0 counter on Balduvian Hydra. Activate only during your upkeep.', "Banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "Banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)\\n{1}{W}: Kjeldoran Knight gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{W}{W}: Kjeldoran Knight gets +0/+2 until end of turn.", 'Black and/or red permanents and spells are colorless sources of damage.', "Black creatures can't attack unless their controller sacrifices a land for each black creature they control that's attacking. (This cost is paid as attackers are declared.)", 'Blocking creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Cast this spell only during combat before blockers are declared.\\nTarget creature can't block this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Cast this spell only during combat before blockers are declared.\\nX can't be greater than the number of snow lands you control.\\nChoose X target attacking creatures. For each of those creatures, its controller may pay {1} or {2}. If that player doesn't, destroy that creature at end of combat. If that player pays only {1}, prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by that creature this combat.", "Cast this spell only during your turn and only during combat before blockers are declared.\\nYou choose which creatures block this combat and how those creatures block.\\nWhenever a creature attacks and isn't blocked this combat, untap it and remove it from combat.", "Cast this spell only if you control a snow land.\\nCumulative upkeep {2} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nCreatures with flying don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'Change the target of target spell with a single target.', 'Change the text of target spell or permanent by replacing all instances of one color word with another. (For example, you may change "target black spell" to "target blue spell." This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Choose a card name. Exile the top six cards of your library, then reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a card with the chosen name. Put that card into your hand and exile all other cards revealed this way.', "Choose one —\\n• Counter target spell if it's blue.\\n• Destroy target permanent if it's blue.", "Choose one —\\n• Counter target spell if it's red.\\n• Destroy target permanent if it's red.", "Choose target creature. At this turn's next end of combat, destroy all creatures that blocked or were blocked by it this turn.", "Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Counter target spell unless its controller pays {X}. If that player doesn't, they tap all lands with mana abilities they control and lose all unspent mana.", 'Counter target spell.', "Creatures with landwalk abilities can be blocked as though they didn't have those abilities.", "Creatures without flying don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player may choose any number of tapped creatures without flying they control and pay {2} for each creature chosen this way. If the player does, untap those creatures.", 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAll creatures get -1/-0.\\n{1}{G}: All creatures get -1/-0 until end of turn.', "Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nCreatures that attacked during their controller's last turn can't attack.", "Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nFlow of Maggots can't be blocked by non-Wall creatures.", "Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt by instant and sorcery spells.\\nCreatures with flying don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhenever an opponent casts a noncreature spell, you may draw a card unless that player pays {4}.', 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{1}: Soldevi Simulacrum gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{T}: Put a music counter on target creature. If it doesn\'t have "At the beginning of your upkeep, destroy this creature unless you pay {1} for each music counter on it," it gains that ability.', 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{U}, Discard a card: Draw a card.', 'Cumulative upkeep {1}{U}{U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nIf tapped for mana, Plains produce {R}, Swamps produce {G}, Mountains produce {W}, and Forests produce {B} instead of any other type.', 'Cumulative upkeep {2} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAs Illusionary Terrain enters the battlefield, choose two basic land types.\\nBasic lands of the first chosen type are the second chosen type.', "Cumulative upkeep {2} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, Cold Snap deals damage to that player equal to the number of snow lands they control.", 'Cumulative upkeep {2} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nIf a land is tapped for mana, it produces colorless mana instead of any other type.', 'Cumulative upkeep {2} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhen Illusions of Grandeur enters the battlefield, you gain 20 life.\\nWhen Illusions of Grandeur leaves the battlefield, you lose 20 life.', 'Cumulative upkeep {3} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nIf tapped for mana, Plains produce {R}, Islands produce {G}, Swamps produce {W}, Mountains produce {U}, and Forests produce {B} instead of any other type.', "Cumulative upkeep {U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, choose a land type. Illusionary Presence gains landwalk of the chosen type until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a land of that type.)", 'Cumulative upkeep {U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nGreen creatures have "Cumulative upkeep {1}."', 'Cumulative upkeep {U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhenever an Island is tapped for mana, its controller may add an additional {U}. If that Island is snow, its controller may add an additional {U}{U} instead. Spend this mana only to pay cumulative upkeep costs.', 'Cumulative upkeep {U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{1}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', "Cumulative upkeep—Pay 2 life. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhen Glacial Chasm enters the battlefield, sacrifice a land.\\nCreatures you control can't attack.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to you.", 'Cumulative upkeep—Pay {B} and 1 life. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nIf a land is tapped for mana, it produces {B} instead of any other type.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nBanding (If any creatures with banding you control are blocking a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nDrift of the Dead's power and toughness are each equal to the number of snow lands you control.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying\\n{U}: Thunder Wall gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nSacrifice Tinder Wall: Add {R}{R}.\\n{R}, Sacrifice Tinder Wall: It deals 2 damage to target creature it's blocking.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{1}: Snow Fortress gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{1}: Snow Fortress gets +0/+1 until end of turn.\\n{3}: Snow Fortress deals 1 damage to target creature without flying that's attacking you.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{G}: Regenerate Wall of Pine Needles.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{R}: Wall of Lava gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", 'Defender, flying, first strike\\nCumulative upkeep {U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', "Defender\\n{3}: Walking Wall gets +3/-1 until end of turn and can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender. Activate only once each turn.", 'Destroy X target snow lands.', "Destroy all Plains. For each land destroyed this way, Stench of Evil deals 1 damage to that land's controller unless they pay {2}.", "Destroy all artifacts, creatures, and lands. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy all enchantments or all nonwhite enchantments.', 'Destroy all white permanents.', "Destroy target Wall. It can't be regenerated. Word of Blasting deals damage equal to that Wall's mana value to the Wall's controller.", 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact.', "Destroy target creature unless its controller pays life equal to its toughness. A creature destroyed this way can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target land.', "Destroy target land. If that land was a snow land, Icequake deals 1 damage to that land's controller.", 'Destroy target land. If that land was a snow land, you gain 1 life.', "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", "Dire Wolves has banding as long as you control a Plains. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", 'Draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.', 'Each player loses a third of their life, then discards a third of the cards in their hand, then sacrifices a third of the creatures they control, then sacrifices a third of the lands they control. Round up each time.', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has fear. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\n{G}: Regenerate enchanted creature. (The next time that creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", 'Enchant creature card in a graveyard\\nWhen Dance of the Dead enters the battlefield, if it\'s on the battlefield, it loses "enchant creature card in a graveyard" and gains "enchant creature put onto the battlefield with Dance of the Dead." Put enchanted creature card onto the battlefield tapped under your control and attach Dance of the Dead to it. When Dance of the Dead leaves the battlefield, that creature\'s controller sacrifices it.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and doesn\'t untap during its controller\'s untap step.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature\'s controller, that player may pay {1}{B}. If the player does, untap that creature.', "Enchant creature you control\\nWhenever enchanted creature attacks and isn't blocked, you may have it assign no combat damage this turn. If you do, defending player discards a card at random.", 'Enchant creature\\nAll creatures able to block enchanted creature do so.', 'Enchant creature\\nAs Chromatic Armor enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nChromatic Armor enters the battlefield with a sleight counter on it.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to enchanted creature by sources of the last chosen color.\\n{X}: Put a sleight counter on Chromatic Armor and choose a color. X is the number of sleight counters on Chromatic Armor.', 'Enchant creature\\nAs Prismatic Ward enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to enchanted creature by sources of the chosen color.', "Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, that player may pay any amount of mana. Errant Minion deals 2 damage to that player. Prevent X of that damage, where X is the amount of mana that player paid this way.", "Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, that player may pay {3}. If they don't, Mind Whip deals 2 damage to that player and you tap that creature.", 'Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Binding Grasp unless you pay {1}{U}.\\nYou control enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+1.', "Enchant creature\\nCumulative upkeep {G} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, Maddening Wind deals 2 damage to that player.", "Enchant creature\\nCumulative upkeep {R} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nEnchanted creature's controller can't cast creature spells.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked by black creatures.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as an opponent controls a black permanent.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked by blue creatures.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as an opponent controls a blue permanent.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked by green creatures.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as an opponent controls a green permanent.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked by red creatures.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as an opponent controls a red permanent.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked by white creatures.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as an opponent controls a white permanent.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+2 and can't be the target of spells.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+2.\\n{R}: Enchanted creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+0 and has flying and first strike.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\n{W}: Enchanted creature gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+0.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, put a -0/-1 counter on that creature.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+0 and can only attack alone.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -X/-Y. If that creature is attacking, X is the number of snow lands defending player controls. Otherwise, X is the number of snow lands its controller controls. Y is equal to X or to enchanted creature's toughness minus 1, whichever is smaller.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has banding. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding a player controls are blocking or being blocked by a creature, that player divides that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has flying.\\nEnchanted creature has first strike as long as it's blocking and you control a snow land.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has menace. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has swampwalk. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", 'Enchant creature\\nFylgja enters the battlefield with four healing counters on it.\\nRemove a healing counter from Fylgja: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to enchanted creature this turn.\\n{2}{W}: Put a healing counter on Fylgja.', "Enchant creature\\nWhen Krovikan Fetish enters the battlefield, draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.", "Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature becomes tapped, Seizures deals 3 damage to that creature's controller unless that player pays {3}.", 'Enchant creature\\n{B}, Pay 1 life: Enchanted creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate no more than three times each turn.', 'Enchant land you control\\nCumulative upkeep {1}{U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn."', 'Enchant land you control\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn."', 'Enchant land you control\\nEnchanted land has "{W}{W}, {T}: Create a 0/1 white Caribou creature token."\\nSacrifice a Caribou token: You gain 1 life.', 'Enchant land you control\\nTap enchanted land: Target blocking creature gets +1/+2 until end of turn. Activate only if enchanted land is untapped.', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Target creature gets +2/+1 until end of turn."', 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional {G}.', 'Enchant land\\nYou control enchanted land.', "Enchant non-Wall creature\\nEnchanted creature has first strike and trample.\\nAt the beginning of the end step of enchanted creature's controller, destroy that creature if it didn't attack this turn.", 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', 'Fiery Justice deals 5 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets. Target opponent gains 5 life.', 'First strike', "First strike; banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", 'First strike\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, target opponent gains control of Chaos Lord if the number of permanents is even.\\nChaos Lord can attack as though it had haste unless it entered the battlefield this turn.', "Flare deals 1 damage to any target.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Flip a coin. If you win the flip, you gain 1 life and target opponent loses 1 life, and you decide whether to flip again. If you lose the flip, you lose 1 life and that opponent gains 1 life, and that player decides whether to flip again. Double the life stakes with each flip.', 'Flying, trample', "Flying; first strike; banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", 'Flying\\nCumulative upkeep {U} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', "Flying\\nMenace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", 'Flying\\nWhenever Abyssal Specter deals damage to a player, that player discards a card.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Sibilant Spirit attacks, defending player may draw a card.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Seraph this turn dies, put that card onto the battlefield under your control at the beginning of the next end step. Sacrifice the creature when you lose control of Seraph.', 'Flying\\n{G}: Regenerate Yavimaya Gnats.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Storm Spirit deals 2 damage to target creature.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target creature you control with toughness 2 or less gets +1/+1 and gains flying until end of turn. When Phantasmal Mount leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice that creature. When the creature leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice Phantasmal Mount.', "For each artifact or creature card in target opponent's graveyard, add {C} and you gain 1 life.", "Foul Familiar can't block.\\n{B}, Pay 1 life: Return Foul Familiar to its owner's hand.", "Gorilla Pack can't attack unless defending player controls a Forest.\\nWhen you control no Forests, sacrifice Gorilla Pack.", "Green creatures can't attack unless their controller sacrifices a land for each green creature they control that's attacking. (This cost is paid as attackers are declared.)", 'Green creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nNongreen creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Haste\\n{B}: Return Ashen Ghoul from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep and only if three or more creature cards are above Ashen Ghoul.', "Hipparion can't block creatures with power 3 or greater unless you pay {1}.", 'Hurricane deals X damage to each creature with flying and each player.', 'Iceberg enters the battlefield with X ice counters on it.\\n{3}: Put an ice counter on Iceberg.\\nRemove an ice counter from Iceberg: Add {C}.', "Incinerate deals 3 damage to any target. A creature dealt damage this way can't be regenerated this turn.", "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", "Jester's Mask enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Jester's Mask: Target opponent puts the cards from their hand on top of their library. Search that player's library for that many cards. That player puts those cards into their hand, then shuffles.", "Land Cap doesn't untap during your untap step if it has a depletion counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove a depletion counter from Land Cap.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Put a depletion counter on Land Cap.", "Lava Burst deals X damage to any target. If Lava Burst would deal damage to a creature, that damage can't be prevented or dealt instead to another permanent or player.", "Lava Tubes doesn't untap during your untap step if it has a depletion counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove a depletion counter from Lava Tubes.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Put a depletion counter on Lava Tubes.", "Lhurgoyf's power is equal to the number of creature cards in all graveyards and its toughness is equal to that number plus 1.", "Look at target player's hand and choose X cards from it. That player discards those cards.", "Look at target player's hand.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Look at the top five cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on top of your library in any order.', "Look at the top three cards of target player's library, then put them back in any order. You may have that player shuffle.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Merieke Ri Berit doesn't untap during your untap step.\\n{T}: Gain control of target creature for as long as you control Merieke Ri Berit. When Merieke Ri Berit leaves the battlefield or becomes untapped, destroy that creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Meteor Shower deals X plus 1 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", "Orcish Conscripts can't attack unless at least two other creatures attack.\\nOrcish Conscripts can't block unless at least two other creatures block.", "Pestilence Rats's power is equal to the number of other Rats on the battlefield. (For example, as long as there are two other Rats on the battlefield, Pestilence Rats's power and toughness are 2/3.)", "Play with your hand revealed.\\nIf you would draw a card, reveal the top card of your library instead. If it's a creature card, put it into your graveyard. Otherwise, draw a card.\\nWhenever a creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return it to your hand.", "Players play with their hands revealed.\\nIf a player would draw a card, they reveal it instead. Then any other player may pay 2 life. If a player does, put that card into its owner's graveyard. Otherwise, that player draws a card.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by target attacking creature this turn.', "Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn. At the beginning of the next end step, put a +0/+1 counter on that creature for each 1 damage prevented this way.', 'Protection from black\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, Minion of Leshrac deals 5 damage to you unless you sacrifice a creature other than Minion of Leshrac. If Minion of Leshrac deals damage to you this way, tap it.\\n{T}: Destroy target creature or land.', 'Protection from black\\n{W}: Order of the White Shield gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{W}{W}: Order of the White Shield gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Protection from white\\n{B}: Knight of Stromgald gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{B}{B}: Knight of Stromgald gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.', 'Pyroclasm deals 2 damage to each creature.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Woolly Spider blocks a creature with flying, Woolly Spider gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'Regenerate target creature.', "Remove Amulet of Quoz from your deck before playing if you're not playing for ante.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Amulet of Quoz: Target opponent may ante the top card of their library. If they don't, you flip a coin. If you win the flip, that player loses the game. If you lose the flip, you lose the game. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Return target creature and all white Auras you own attached to it to their owners' hands.", "River Delta doesn't untap during your untap step if it has a depletion counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove a depletion counter from River Delta.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Put a depletion counter on River Delta.", "Runed Arch enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{X}, {T}, Sacrifice Runed Arch: X target creatures with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", "Sacrifice Goblin Lyre: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, Goblin Lyre deals damage to target opponent or planeswalker equal to the number of creatures you control. If you lose the flip, Goblin Lyre deals damage to you equal to the number of creatures that opponent or that planeswalker's controller controls.", 'Sacrifice a land: You gain 2 life.', 'Sacrifice a snow Mountain: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Skip your draw step.\\nWhenever you discard a card, exile that card from your graveyard.\\nPay 1 life: Exile the top card of your library face down. Put that card into your hand at the beginning of your next end step.', "Snow forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a snow Forest.)", "Snow swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a snow Swamp.)", "Soldevi Golem doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may untap target tapped creature an opponent controls. If you do, untap Soldevi Golem.", "Spend only black and/or red mana on X.\\nSoul Burn deals X damage to any target. You gain life equal to the damage dealt, but not more than the amount of {B} spent on X, the player's life total before the damage was dealt, the planeswalker's loyalty before the damage was dealt, or the creature's toughness.", "Stone Spirit can't be blocked by creatures with flying.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", 'Tap an untapped snow land you control: Karplusan Giant gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Tap target artifact, creature, or land.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", "Target creature can't be regenerated this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target creature gains banding until end of turn. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding a player controls are blocking or being blocked by a creature, that player divides that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target creature gains flying until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Target creature gets +3/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn.', "Target opponent chooses a card in your graveyard. You may pay {G}. If you do, repeat this process except that opponent can't choose a card already chosen for Forgotten Lore. Then put the last chosen card into your hand.", 'Target player chooses three cards from their hand and puts them on top of their library in any order.', "Target player discards a card.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target player mills a card.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Timberline Ridge doesn't untap during your untap step if it has a depletion counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove a depletion counter from Timberline Ridge.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Put a depletion counter on Timberline Ridge.", "Touch of Death deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker. You gain 1 life.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Trample\\nGoblin Mutant can't attack if defending player controls an untapped creature with power 3 or greater.\\nGoblin Mutant can't block creatures with power 3 or greater.", 'Trample\\nPolar Kraken enters the battlefield tapped.\\nCumulative upkeep—Sacrifice a land. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', 'Trample\\nWhenever Aurochs attacks, it gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each other attacking Aurochs.', 'Untap all white creatures you control.\\nWhenever a creature blocks this turn, it gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', "Untap target artifact, creature, or land.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Untap target attacking creature. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by that creature this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Untap target creature an opponent controls and gain control of it until end of turn. That creature gains haste until end of turn. When you lose control of the creature, tap it.', 'Until end of turn, target creature gains haste and "{0}: Untap this creature. Activate only once."\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn\'s upkeep.', "Until end of turn, whenever a creature you control attacks and isn't blocked, you may choose to have it deal damage equal to its power to a target creature. If you do, it assigns no combat damage this turn.", "Veldt doesn't untap during your untap step if it has a depletion counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove a depletion counter from Veldt.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Put a depletion counter on Veldt.", 'Vertigo deals 2 damage to target creature with flying. That creature loses flying until end of turn.', "When Curse of Marit Lage enters the battlefield, tap all Islands.\\nIslands don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'When Hecatomb enters the battlefield, sacrifice Hecatomb unless you sacrifice four creatures.\\nTap an untapped Swamp you control: Hecatomb deals 1 damage to any target.', "When Icy Prison enters the battlefield, exile target creature.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Icy Prison unless any player pays {3}.\\nWhen Icy Prison leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Kjeldoran Dead enters the battlefield, sacrifice a creature.\\n{B}: Regenerate Kjeldoran Dead.', "When Pyknite enters the battlefield, draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'When Tarpan dies, you gain 1 life.', "When Wrath of Marit Lage enters the battlefield, tap all red creatures.\\nRed creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'When you control no Islands, sacrifice Skeleton Ship.\\n{T}: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.', 'Whenever Chub Toad blocks or becomes blocked, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', "Whenever Goblin Snowman blocks, prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by it this turn.\\n{T}: Goblin Snowman deals 1 damage to target creature it's blocking.", 'Whenever Johtull Wurm becomes blocked, it gets -2/-1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.', "Whenever Lim-Dûl's Cohort blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, that creature can't be regenerated this turn.", 'Whenever Márton Stromgald attacks, other attacking creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn for each attacking creature other than Márton Stromgald.\\nWhenever Márton Stromgald blocks, other blocking creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn for each blocking creature other than Márton Stromgald.', "Whenever Orcish Squatters attacks and isn't blocked, you may gain control of target land defending player controls for as long as you control Orcish Squatters. If you do, Orcish Squatters assigns no combat damage this turn.", "Whenever a permanent becomes tapped, put a wind counter on it.\\nIf a permanent with a wind counter on it would untap during its controller's untap step, remove all wind counters from it instead.", "Whenever a player attacks with one or more creatures, destroy all untapped non-Wall creatures that player controls that didn't attack, except for creatures the player hasn't controlled continuously since the beginning of the turn.", 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may pay {3}. If you do, untap target permanent.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may pay {3}. If you do, untap target permanent.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may pay {3}. If you do, untap target permanent.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may pay {3}. If you do, untap target permanent.', 'Whenever a player casts a white spell, you may pay {3}. If you do, untap target permanent.', 'Whenever an Island an opponent controls becomes tapped, you may gain 1 life.', "Whenever an opponent casts a black spell, you may pay {G}{G}. If you do, you draw a card.\\n{G}{G}: Return Freyalise's Charm to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever an opponent casts a creature spell, Soul Barrier deals 2 damage to that player unless they pay {2}.', "Whenever an opponent casts a green spell, you may pay {B}{B}. If you do, look at that player's hand and choose a card from it. The player discards that card.\\n{B}{B}: Return Leshrac's Sigil to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever you lose life, for each 1 life you lost, sacrifice a permanent other than Oath of Lim-Dûl unless you discard a card. (Damage dealt to you causes you to lose life.)\\n{B}{B}: Draw a card.', 'Wiitigo enters the battlefield with six +1/+1 counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a +1/+1 counter on Wiitigo if it has blocked or been blocked since your last upkeep. Otherwise, remove a +1/+1 counter from it.', 'Woolly Mammoths has trample as long as you control a snow land.', "X is the number of artifact and/or creature cards in an opponent's graveyard as you cast this spell.\\nDistribute X +1/+1 counters among any number of target creatures.", "You gain 1 life.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "You may choose not to untap Ice Floe during your untap step.\\n{T}: Tap target creature without flying that's attacking you. It doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Ice Floe remains tapped.", "You may choose not to untap Mole Worms during your untap step.\\n{T}: Tap target land. It doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Mole Worms remains tapped.", '{0}: Hyalopterous Lemure gets -1/-0 and gains flying until end of turn.', "{0}: Return Blinking Spirit to its owner's hand.", "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Barbed Sextant: Add one mana of any color. Draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Skull Catapult deals 2 damage to any target.', "{1}, {T}: Put a charge counter on Jeweled Amulet. Note the type of mana spent to pay this activation cost. Activate only if there are no charge counters on Jeweled Amulet.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Jeweled Amulet: Add one mana of Jeweled Amulet's last noted type.", "{1}, {T}: Return Snow Hound and target green or blue creature you control to their owner's hand.", '{1}, {T}: Tap target artifact, creature, or land.', '{1}, {T}: Target 1/1 creature gets +1/+2 until end of turn.', '{1}: Adarkar Sentinel gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{1}: The next time a black source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a blue source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a green source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a red source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a white source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', "{1}{G}, {T}: Counter target activated ability from an artifact source. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)", '{1}{G}: Folk of the Pines gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{R}: Goblin Ski Patrol gets +2/+0 and gains flying. Its controller sacrifices it at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only once and only if you control a snow Mountain.', "{1}{R}{G}, {T}: Exile Giant Trap Door Spider and target creature without flying that's attacking you.", '{1}{R}{R}: Until end of turn, whenever you cast a black spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Mountain Titan.', '{1}{U}, {T}: Untap target artifact an opponent controls and gain control of it until end of turn. It gains haste until end of turn. When you lose control of the artifact, tap it.', '{1}{U}: Return target white or black creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. That creature gains "Cumulative upkeep {2}." If the creature would leave the battlefield, exile it instead of putting it anywhere else. (At the beginning of its controller\'s upkeep, that player puts an age counter on it, then sacrifices it unless they pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', '{1}{W}: Target green creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{2}, Discard a card at random: Stormbind deals 2 damage to any target.', '{2}, Sacrifice a land: Put a +2/+2 counter on target creature. Activate only during any upkeep step.', '{2}, Sacrifice a snow land: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Jester's Cap: Search target player's library for three cards and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Pit Trap: Destroy target attacking creature without flying. It can't be regenerated.", '{2}, {T}: Target creature gains vigilance until end of turn. Activate only during combat and only if defending player controls a snow land.', '{2}, {T}: Target creature with power 3 or less gains flying until end of turn.', '{2}, {T}: Target snow land is no longer snow.\\n{2}, {T}: Target nonsnow basic land becomes snow.', '{2}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to you this turn.', "{2}: Target creature gains banding until end of turn. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding a player controls are blocking or being blocked by a creature, that player divides that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", '{2}{B}, {T}: Target player discards a card. Activate only during your turn.', '{2}{G}, {T}: Untap target creature.', "{2}{R}, {T}: Choose a land type. Target creature you control gains snow landwalk of the chosen type until end of turn. Return that creature to its owner's hand at the beginning of the next end step. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a snow land of that type.)", '{2}{R}: Target creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{U}{U}: Target creature you control gains flying until end of turn. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.', "{3}, {T}: Choose target non-Wall creature the active player has controlled continuously since the beginning of the turn. That player may pay {X}, where X is that mana value. If they don't pay, the creature attacks this turn if able, and at the beginning of the next end step, destroy it if it didn't attack this turn. Activate only before attackers are declared.", '{3}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library. Until the beginning of your next upkeep, you may play that card.', '{3}, {T}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{3}, {T}: Target creature gains trample until end of turn.', '{3}, {T}: Target creature you control gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Its controller sacrifices it at the beginning of the next end step.', '{3}, {T}: Target player chooses a card name, then reveals the top card of their library. If that card has the chosen name, that player puts it into their hand. Otherwise, they put it into their graveyard and Vexing Arcanix deals 2 damage to them.', "{3}: Look at the top three cards of target player's library, then put them back in any order.", '{3}: The next time Mercenaries would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage. Any player may activate this ability.', '{3}{G}, {T}: You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.', '{4}, {T}: Attach target Aura attached to a creature to another creature.', '{4}, {T}: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{B}: Hoar Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{B}: Until end of turn, Bone Shaman gains "Creatures dealt damage by Bone Shaman this turn can\'t be regenerated this turn."', '{R}, {T}: Look at the top eight cards of your library. Exile four of them at random, then put the rest on top of your library in any order.', '{R}: Flame Spirit gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{R}: Grizzled Wolverine gets +2/+0 until end of turn. Activate only during the declare blockers step, only if at least one creature is blocking Grizzled Wolverine, and only once each turn.', '{R}{G}: Shambling Strider gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', "{R}{R}, {T}: Target creature can't be regenerated this turn.\\n{B}{B}{R}, {T}: Regenerate target black or green creature.\\n{R}{G}{G}, {T}: Regenerate target black or green creature.", "{R}{R}, {T}: Target creature you control can't be blocked this turn. Destroy it and Goblin Sappers at end of combat.\\n{R}{R}{R}{R}, {T}: Target creature you control can't be blocked this turn. Destroy it at end of combat.", '{T}, Discard a nonblack card: Draw a card.\\n{T}, Discard a black card: Draw two cards, then discard one of them.', '{T}, Pay 1 life: Counter target black spell.', '{T}, Pay 1 life: Counter target white spell.', '{T}, Sacrifice Gangrenous Zombies: Gangrenous Zombies deals 1 damage to each creature and each player. If you control a snow Swamp, Gangrenous Zombies deals 2 damage to each creature and each player instead.', "{T}, Sacrifice Urza's Bauble: Look at a card at random in target player's hand. You draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{T}, Sacrifice a Forest: Add three mana in any combination of {R} and/or {G}.', '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\n{1}{U}{U}, Sacrifice a creature: Counter target creature spell.', "{T}, Sacrifice a red or white creature: Freyalise Supplicant deals damage to any target equal to half the sacrificed creature's power, rounded down.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Sulfurous Springs deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Brushland deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Karplusan Forest deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Adarkar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to activate abilities of artifacts.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Add {G}{G}.', '{T}: Add {U} or {C}{U}. Spend this mana only to pay cumulative upkeep costs.', '{T}: All combat damage that would be dealt to you by unblocked creatures this turn is dealt to Kjeldoran Royal Guard instead.', '{T}: Centaur Archer deals 1 damage to target creature with flying.', '{T}: Change the text of target white enchantment you control that doesn\'t have cumulative upkeep by replacing all instances of one color word with another. (For example, you may change "black creatures can\'t attack" to "blue creatures can\'t attack.") That enchantment gains "Cumulative upkeep {1}." (At the beginning of its controller\'s upkeep, that player puts an age counter on it, then sacrifices it unless they pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', "{T}: Choose two target blocked attacking creatures. If each of those creatures could be blocked by all creatures that the other is blocked by, each creature that's blocking exactly one of those attacking creatures stops blocking it and is blocking the other attacking creature. Activate only during the declare blockers step.", "{T}: Destroy target permanent you own. It can't be regenerated.", '{T}: Karplusan Yeti deals damage equal to its power to target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power to Karplusan Yeti.', '{T}: Orcish Cannoneers deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.', "{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn. If it's a green creature, prevent the next 2 damage instead.", '{T}: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn. When that creature leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice Kjeldoran Guard. Activate only during combat and only if defending player controls no snow lands.', '{T}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. When that creature leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice Kjeldoran Elite Guard. Activate only during combat.', "{T}: Target land becomes a Swamp until its controller's next untap step.", "{T}: Target snow land becomes a 2/2 creature until end of turn. It's still a land.", "{T}: Untap target blue creature.\\n{T}: Choose target non-Wall creature the active player has controlled continuously since the beginning of the turn. That creature attacks this turn if able. Destroy it at the beginning of the next end step if it didn't attack this turn. Activate only before attackers are declared.", '{T}: Untap target land.', '{T}: Zuran Spellcaster deals 1 damage to any target.', '{U}: Counter target spell that targets Mistfolk.', '{U}: Sea Spirit gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{W}, Sacrifice an enchantment: Destroy target enchantment.\\n{3}{U}{U}: Counter target enchantment spell.', "{W}{W}: Return target nonsnow land you control to its owner's hand.", "{X}, {T}: You may exile a nonland card from your hand. You may cast that card for as long as it remains exiled. Put a charge counter on Ice Cauldron and note the type and amount of mana spent to pay this activation cost. Activate only if there are no charge counters on Ice Cauldron.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Ice Cauldron: Add Ice Cauldron's last noted type and amount of mana. Spend this mana only to cast the last card exiled with Ice Cauldron."]
flavor: ['"A good Tarpan will serve you, faithful and true. A bad one will kick you in the head."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"A mage must be precise as well as potent; cautious, as well as clever."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"A mind in agony is a sparrow without wings."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"A minion given over to Tevesh Szat is a stronger minion gained."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"A resourceful mage has many sources of information. The best one is your foe."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"AIIIEEEE!"\\n—Ib Halfheart, Goblin Tactician', '"Ach! Hans, run! It\'s the Lhurgoyf!"\\n—Saffi Eriksdotter, last words', '"Although my official log will state there is no evidence pointing to the existence of the Mistfolk, my certainty is lessened by the cursed consistency of the expedition\'s eyewitness accounts."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"As we followed the ice wall, we had the distinct feeling of being watched. Many of the party wanted to turn back."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"Barbarian raids were a concern to those living in the northwest provinces, but the Skyknights never dealt with the problem in a systematic way. They thought of the Balduvians as an \'amusing model\' of their forebears\' culture."\\n—*Kjeldor: Ice Civilization*', '"Before you release a Wolverine from the trap, make sure it\'s really dead."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Bind me to thee, my soul to thine. I am your servant and your slave. I shall hunger for your word and thirst for your blessing. Blood for blood, flesh for flesh, Leshrac, my lord."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Blasted amateurs! Doesn\'t the queen think we can fight well enough on our own?"\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Capturing this specimen was not easy. Study it well, that you someday might be as versatile."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Centaurs will kill our Aesthir if they can; they\'ve always been enemies. Destroy the horse-people on sight."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"Come to us, with your lightning. Come to us, with your thunder. Serve us with your strength, and smite our foes with your power."\\n—Steinar Icefist, Balduvian Shaman', '"Daughter, it is now your turn to hunt the Tiger, and make a blanket of its fur."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Daughter, on the day you have killed your Pale Bear, then will I give you your true name."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Divine gifts are granted to those who are worthy."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Do we know what we\'re doing? Yes—the will of Freyalise."\\n—Laina of the Elvish Council', '"Don\'t look at it! Maybe it\'ll go away!"\\n—Ib Halfheart, Goblin Tactician', '"Eenie, meenie, minie, moe . . . oh, why not all of them?"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Even the bravest of warriors yet knows the dark clutch of fright upon his stalwart heart."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Even the ground is our friend."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Even the highest mountain can be ground to dust."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"Faith in Freyalise has given me the gift, not the curse, of unprecedented longevity."\\n—Laina of the Elvish Council', '"Few of us left, now. Confounded Yeti have opened all the vents. We\'d best hide here with the weapons."\\n—Perena Deepcutter, Dwarven Armorer', '"Finally we understand the lesson of our home: loss begets renewal."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Flourishing during the Ice Age, these Wurms were the bane of all Kjeldorans. Their great size and ferocity made them the subject of countless nightmares—they embodied the worst of the Ice Age."\\n—*Kjeldor: Ice Civilization*', '"Folklore has it that to capture a Mountain Goat is a sign of divine blessing. I just know it\'s a sign that dinner is on the way."\\n—Klazina Jansdotter, Leader of the Order of the Sacred Torch', '"For those of courage, even the sky holds no limit."\\n—Arnjlot Olasson, Sky Mage', '"Freyalise has cleansed our bodies and minds of the plagues of Kjeldor; all she asks in return is that we keep pure our newly given home in Fyndhorn."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"From the mouths of my servants, my voice shall emerge to shake the souls of my foes."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Fyndhorn is our home."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Get up, blast you! They\'re attacking! Why are you all so slow?"\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"Give me a thousand such Warriors and I could change the world."\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Give me wings to fly and speed to strike. In return, the glory I earn shall be yours."\\n—Steinar Icefist, Balduvian Shaman', '"Heed the lessons of our time: the forms of water may move the land itself and hold captive the fires within."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"Here in Fyndhorn, the goddess Freyalise is generous to her children."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Here in Fyndhorn, where Freyalise\'s power is strongest, the forest has its own opinion."\\n—Laina of the Elvish Council', '"Honorable in battle, generous in death."\\n—Motto of the Kjeldoran Royal Guard', '"How did I ever let myself get talked into this project?"\\n—Toothlicker Harj, Orcish Captain', '"I am older than any Elder Druid before me, and still no child has been born with the Mark to take my place. When will the wheel turn?"\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"I breathed deeply, and suddenly I knew not who or where I was."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"I can\'t believe they expect me to fight with this rabble. A Goblin in a big mask sends \'em running for cover."\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"I dispute Relicbane\'s hysterical allegations, Commissioner, but it is true that these artifacts can be dangerous."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"I don\'t understand the appeal of keeping these things as pets, unless you want your children eaten."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"I have been a warrior for over four hundred years, and yet each generation of Kjeldorans teaches me new tricks. There can be no better allies."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"I have my faith, and I have my prayers. But if push comes to shove, I\'ve also got a little something extra."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"I have seen the faces of my dead friends among that grim band, and I can bear no more."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"I have seen the true path. I will not warm myself by the fire—I will become the flame."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"I implore you not to forget the horrors of the past. You would have us start the Brothers\' War anew!"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"I reeled from the blow, and then suddenly, I knew exactly what to do. Within moments, victory was mine."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter,\\nKjeldoran Royal Mage', '"I saw the wizard gesturing, but I didn\'t guess his plan until my Aesthir cried out and went into a dive."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"I strive for elegance and speed in my work."\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"I thought the day had brought enough horrors for our ragged band, but the night was far worse."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"I was shocked when I first saw the aftermath of the Yavimaya Valley disaster. The raging waters had swept away trees, bridges, and even houses. My healers had much work to do."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"I will go to any length to achieve my goal. Eternal life is worth any sacrifice."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"I wouldn\'t advise using it with a Woolly Mammoth, but it\'s quite appropriate for many other beasts."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"I\'ve been insulted by drunks in a hundred inns, but never as skillfully or annoyingly as by those blasted Brownies."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"I\'ve seen a larger Erne knock a Giant to the ground and stay airborne. They move not with the wind, but as the wind."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"If we do our duty and uphold our honor, Kjeldor shall stand for a thousand years."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"If you do it right, they\'ll never know what hit them."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"If you\'d been there, you would\'ve run from that deer, too!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"If you\'re starving, eat your horses, your dead, or yourself—but *never* eat your dog."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"In the thick of battle, you must keep your wits about you. Yelling a lot helps, too."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"It is Freyalise, walking on the world."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"It is our third day of travel on the Yavimaya River, and still these creatures plague us. Davin Lansson, our naturalist, has facetiously labeled them \'gnats,\' and the name has stuck."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"It is the changing of perception that is important."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"It rose above our heads, above the ship, and still higher yet. No foggy, ice-laden sea in the world could frighten me more."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"It was big. Really, really, big. No, bigger than that. It was *big!*"\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"It was in Urza\'s journals that I finally found the secret at the core of the summonings."\\n—Journal, author unknown', '"It\'s a thankless job, and you\'ll probably die in an explosion. But the pay is pretty good."\\n—Toothlicker Harj, Orcish Captain', '"It\'s amazing how scared a city kid can get at a dog. Now, of course, I\'d cross Terisiare alone, and keep no watch if I had a pack of greys hanging on my flanks as I went."\\n—Oddveig Ulfsson, caravan scout', '"It\'s no Ornithopter, but then I\'m no Urza."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"It\'s the pokey bits that hurt the most."\\n—Ib Halfheart, Goblin Tactician', '"Join me in the place of power, you risen dead. Join me where the waters weep and the trees have no hearts."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Just the thing for those pesky water mages."\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Keep your chainmail, warrior. I have my own form of protection."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Kjeldor must be supreme at any cost."\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Kjeldorans should rule supreme, and to the rest, death!"\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Know your foes\' strengths as well as their weaknesses."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Leaves more room for the big ones to fight in, you know."\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Leshrac, my liege, grant me the power I am due."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Let any who doubt the evil of using the ancient devices look at this infernal machine. What manner of fiend would design such a sadistic device?"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Let go your fury, and hone your anger. Become the fist of Freyalise!"\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Let the past be the past. Do not call up that which you cannot put down. Destroy that which destroyed us, so long ago."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Let them close the gates of Krov from dusk until dawn if they so choose. It matters not. My fiends shall yet rend their flesh from their bones."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Let them see what is not there and feel what does not touch them. When they no longer trust their senses, that is the time to strike."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Let those who bear the brand receive no shelter, no kindness, and no comfort from our people."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Let us remember brave Jarkeld and his troops, who perished in the Adarkar Wastes so long ago."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Living side by side with the Elves for so long leaves me with no doubt that we serve the same goddess."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Magic overused can freeze the mind. Creativity is more important than power."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"Mammoths may be good to ride on, but they\'re certainly bad to fall off of!"\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"May the bounty of Kjeld enrich your days."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"May the forces that took Argoth beneath the waves never come among us again."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"My Aesthir is my most trusted ally. We fight as one and live as one, and we will die as one."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"My foes serve me twice: in dying, and in death."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"My mind and spirit are one—a barrier not readily passed."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"Never cross a Pyknite, if you value your scalp."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"No one in her right mind would venture off the coast of Kjeldor during this season."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"Nothing is as it seems."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Now *there\'s* something you don\'t see every day."\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"On this site where Kjeld\'s blood was spilled, let none raise a fist or deny a beggar."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Once, our people could call down the storm itself to do our bidding."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"One day you, too, shall drink the blood of your foes. It is something to look forward to."\\n—Toothlicker Harj, Orcish Captain', '"Only the foolish fear Foxfire."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Open the gates, and bid them enter."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Ouphes love trinkets and love to take them apart. I only wish they wouldn\'t do so with the magical ones."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"Our Elvish Hunter Taaveti led us swiftly along hidden paths through the dense forest. We caught the Orcs from behind, and completely by surprise."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"Our friends of the forest take many forms, yet all serve the will of Freyalise."\\n—Laina of the Elvish Council', '"Our world has not felt her thundering steps in lifetimes, but Marit Lage\'s presence is still with us."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Overkill? This isn\'t a game of Kick-the-Ouphe!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Perhaps this time the power of the artificers shall be used wisely."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Rangers not trained by the Elves just aren\'t the same."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"Relax. I\'m sure it\'s just a snake hissing."\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Serve me, and live forever."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Shall we turn away a worthy soul because his parents were peasants? I think not."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"Sheathe your sword, warrior, lest ye fall on it when stricken."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"So great is its power, only the chosen can wield it and live."\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"So large and so quiet—a combination best avoided."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"Someone once said that Hipparions are to Warriors what Aesthir are to Skyknights. Don\'t believe it."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"Sometimes even the smallest boon can save a life."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Sometimes, a soul is not ready to complete its journey to the next world."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Stand your ground, troops! This shall be our finest hour!"\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox, last words', '"Strength in numbers? Right."\\n—Ib Halfheart, Goblin Tactician', '"Take their dead, and entomb them in the snow. Risen, they shall serve a new purpose."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Take this item, for instance. How would it destroy us, Relicbane?"\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"That which does not bend to the will of Freyalise shall surely break."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"The Dryads told us to stay, as no new horrors would come when it was so cold. Three of us left anyway. The rest believed their lies, and their skeletons weren\'t found until the thaw."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"The Elementalists\' talents could be useful if turned to other purposes."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"The Elves train our healers, and we keep the Orcs at bay. Most Elvish bargains aren\'t as fair."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"The Goblins would kill to get ahold of this one."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"The Kjeldorans keep the Orcs at bay and we train their healers. Most human bargains aren\'t as fair."\\n—Laina of the Elvish Council', '"The Lemures had barely taken wing when the sky roared with thunder. The swarm of little beasts wavered, divided, and fell, crashing to the earth."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"The Lemures looked harmless, until they descended on my troops. Within moments, only bones remained."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"The Shaman waved the staff, and the land itself went mad."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"The Shamans of Marit Lage do her bidding in secret, but they do it gladly."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"The Titans claimed to draw strength from the rocks, but I suspect them of some darker allegiance."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"The creature we fought in the western waste was doubly dangerous: mortally wounded, it rebounded and attacked again."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"The drawing of maps is fruitless in the west near the ice walls; the very earth is formless."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"The dreams of a child fulfilled:\\nthe wind on my brow,\\nthe air \'neath my feet."\\n—Arnjlot Olasson, Sky Mage', '"The duel was going badly for me, and Zur thought I was finished. He boasted that he would eat my soul—but all he ate were his words."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"The filthy towns of Kjeldor are no place for anyone to live. Fyndhorn is our home now."\\n—Kolbjörn, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"The fire of justice burns like nothing else."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"The folk of the Karplusan Mountains are impossible to ambush."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"The fortress is not what it seems."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"The pass was completely blocked by the avalanche; we\'re forced to turn back. Nevertheless, we\'ve gone farther and seen more than any before us."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"The potential for change lies in all things. Know a thing\'s nature, know its possibilities, and know it anew."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"The power of flight has but one equal in battle: surprise. Understanding how to use both is the key to victory."\\n—Arnjlot Olasson, Sky Mage', '"The scavengers who first found it called it the \'Bone Crank.\' Not a bad name, I\'d say."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"The sea gives up her dead as easily as the soil."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"The so-called Barbarians will not respect us for our military might—they will respect us for our honor."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"The spirit of the flame is the spirit of change."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"The spirit of the stone is the spirit of strength."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"The very earth seemed alive and made a sound like the writhing of the damned."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"The very lands of Balduvia are alive."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"The weak shall fall. The strong shall remain."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"There is no nobler creature in all of Terisiare."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"There is no shame in solitude. The lone Knight may succeed where a hundred founder."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"There will come soft rains, and spring shall be amongst us, a welcome friend."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"There\'s more than one way to skin an Ouphe—or thwart a mage."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"There\'s nothing I like better than watching a street full of soldiers kicking down the doors of the guilty and the impure."\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"These Sorcerers always seem to have another surprise up their sleeves."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"These traps are truly a symbol of great cruelty and sinister cunning."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"These, of all spells, must have common components I can isolate and use."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"They aren\'t the brightest or the quickest of Giants. For that matter, the same holds true if you compare them to rocks."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"They shall kill those whom once they loved."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"They\'re a hardy bunch, but I\'d still bet that they just slept through the worst of the cold times."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"This is the fun part!"\\n—Ib Halfheart, Goblin Tactician', '"This school was founded in secret, operates in secret, and exists for the teaching of secrets. Those who would alter reality must first escape it."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"This shield is a true rarity: an artifact whose purpose is obvious."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"This was quite possibly the least pleasant occurrence on the entire expedition."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"Those Foxes are wily, swift, and ferocious. They are the warriors of the snows."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"Those who do not ride the wind on Aesthir still command loyalty and respect."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"To bring her down we must be on all sides at once—leave one avenue open and we\'ll all be dead."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"To visit the sky requires bravery, and thought, and little else. To master the sky requires the binding of *its* masters, and little else."\\n—Arnjlot Olasson, Sky Mage', '"Too many of us have died in the explosions that wrack these hills."\\n—Klazina Jansdotter, Leader of the Order of the Sacred Torch', '"Trust in the power of stone. Stone is strong; stone shatters swords; stone breaks bones. Trust in stone."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Two of my Warriors found that the creature was dangerous not only in combat, but also in simple proximity."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"Unearthly and invisible fibers emanate from this sphere, entangling all who draw near."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Virtue has its rewards, as does its opposite."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Walk slowly when in the nether world, and seek that which calls."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Walls? What walls?"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"We are Kjeldorans no more."\\n—Zur the Enchanter', '"We are farther west than any could have imagined possible, but I still wish to press on. Unfortunately, huge walls of ice block further travel. We can\'t believe they are natural."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"We could feel the Shaman\'s power, as surely as we felt the storm."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"We could see the horizon blacken with the great beasts, but it was too late. The icefield offered no immediate safety, but luckily most of us reached a crevasse in which we could take cover."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"We encountered the Sentinels in the wastes, near no living thing. Their purpose was inscrutable."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"We found this staff useful on our visit to this very commission. Would Relicbane prefer we had been slain by Lim-Dûl\'s horrors?"\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"We have joined with the Druids of the Juniper Order. Our faith is one."\\n—Laina of the Elvish Council', '"We learned this at a dear price: once you cross the great river, get through the Yavimaya forest at top speed."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"We need not fear the forces of the air; I\'ve yet to see a Spider without an appetite."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"We shall oppose Lim-Dûl and his forces by any means necessary, even if the very earth be torn asunder."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', '"We were chasing Lim-Dûl when the ridge in front of us suddenly crumbled. I can\'t believe it was mere coincidence."\\n—Lucilde Fiksdotter, Leader of the Order of the White Shield', '"We were not meant to have such terrible things. They should be left where we found them, if not destroyed!"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"What I want, I take."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"What can be a stronger shield than concealment? Have you ever defeated an enemy you didn\'t know existed?"\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"What do you do then? Run. Run very fast. Don\'t stop until you see the camp—or a bigger Giant."\\n—Toothlicker Harj, Orcish Captain', '"What is real can be unreal."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"What was yours is mine. Your land, your people, and now your life."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"What\'s that smell?"\\n—Perena Deepcutter, Dwarven Armorer', '"When the earth shakes, and their animals are swallowed up by the ground, perhaps they will think twice before attacking again."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"Who needs the sun when you\'ve got me around?"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Why do we trade with those despicable Elves? You don\'t live in forests, you burn them!"\\n—Avram Garrisson, Leader of the Knights of Stromgald', '"Will not the mountains quake and hills melt at the coming of the darkness? Share this vision with your enemies, Lim-Dûl, and they shall wither."\\n—Leshrac, Walker of Night', '"With a bow like this, the hunting is always good."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"With the proper equipment and caution, one can travel anywhere."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"With this marvel, even the weak have a fighting chance!"\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Worlds turn in crucial moments of decision. Make your choice."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"Yes, I think \'toast\' is an appropriate description."\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Yes, the Farmers keep our soldiers fed. But why do they have to make every battlefield a pigpen?"\\n—Toothlicker Harj, Orcish Captain', '"You have almost completed your four years, my son. Soon you shall be a Skyknight."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skyknight', 'Abandon not your faith when others abandon you.', 'An end to reason, an end to order. Forget all that has been.', "Chub Toad, Chub Toad\\nAt the door.\\nRun away quick\\nOr you'll run no more.\\n—Traditional children's rhyme", 'Dread Marit Lage lies dreaming, not dead.', "Freyalise forbid that any stranger should wander into the Striders' territory.", "Freyalise's tears bring life and renewal, though they also bring trouble.", 'If only it had three brains, too.', 'In ashes are the gems of history.', 'Masters who sacrifice for servants will receive the gift of loyalty.', 'Never underestimate the power of the soul unleashed.', 'Not wind, but the breath of the dead.', 'One Auroch may feed a village, but a herd will flatten it.', 'One foot in the grave, firmly planted.', 'Rattle me bones as I cross the floor\\nAnd the bones in your grave will rattle no more.', 'Remove the guardians to ensure your victory.', 'Slow and steady wins the race.', 'Some Krovikans find strength in the ears and eyes of their victims and wear such fetishes into battle.', 'That which lasts longest serves best.', 'The power of the forest takes a hundred forms. Some are more surprising than others.', 'The star that burns twice as bright burns half as long.', 'The winged helms of the Guard are put on for pageants—but taken off for war.', 'They look human— until they bleed.', "Up and down,\\nover and through,\\nback around—\\nthe joke's on you.", 'Us hungry, need food . . . . Lots of books . . . . Hmm . . . .', 'Warmth is life; heat is peace.', 'Who knows from whence the winter comes?']
artist: ['Allen Williams', 'Amy Weber', 'Amy Weber & Tom Wänerstrand', 'Andi Rusu', 'Anson Maddocks', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Bryon Wackwitz', 'Christopher Rush', 'Cornelius Brudi', 'Dameon Willich', 'Dan Frazier', 'Daniel Gelon', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Drew Tucker', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Harold McNeill', 'Heather Hudson', 'James Ernest', 'Jeff A. Menges', 'Julie Baroh', 'Justin Hampton', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Ken Meyer, Jr.', 'Liz Danforth', 'Liz Danforth & Douglas Shuler', 'Margaret Organ-Kean', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Melissa A. Benson', 'Mike Kimble', 'Mike Raabe', 'Nicola Leonard', 'NéNé Thomas', 'NéNé Thomas & Catherine Buck', 'NéNé Thomas & Phillip Mosness', 'Pat Lewis', 'Pete Venters', 'Phil Foglio', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Thomas', 'Rick Emond', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ruth Thompson', 'Sandra Everingham', 'Tom Wänerstrand']
